--- body ---

## Context

The conductor's work has landed one fork branch per tranche, by the
tracker's own design (0550: "one fork branch per tranche; each lands
alone, none commits the next"). That worked while the tranches were
sequential. It stopped being true at tranche 3: 0553 and 0556 were built
in parallel off `tranche-2-conductor-election`, and neither is an
ancestor of the other.

Every remaining ticket in the family needs them together:

- **0565** calls `streamFullText`'s `onWindow` callback (tranche 3) and
  writes through `Ledger.putSlab` / `putEntry` / `putPassage` /
  `indexText` (schema branch). It cannot be written against either
  branch alone.
- **0554**'s embed worker needs both the extract stage's work orders and
  the passages the schema branch defines.
- **0566** is the assembly, and reads as though one checkout already
  held all of it.

This ticket is that tree, and nothing more: no new behaviour, no new
tests beyond what the merge requires to stay green.

## Blocked by, and why

**Both blockers are gone, and the reason they were filed is worth
keeping.** This ticket was `Blocked-by: 0553` because tranche 3 was
parked with two confirmed concurrency blockers (PR #156's parking
comment, 2026-09-01), and merging it forward would have carried both
into the base every later tranche builds on. 0553 was resumed and closed
the same day: `tranche-3-extract-shim` at `da3be32` has the ownership
guard on completion and the envelope-closed check, mutation-verified.
0567 — the ledger half of blocker 1 — landed in that same commit rather
than separately, which is what it asked for if 0553 resumed first, so
the "landing it first is cheaper, the conflict region is the same file"
note is settled: `ledger.ts` carries both changes already.

What survives for whoever merges, and it is now more than adjacency:
**0567 was built twice, in parallel, on two fork branches** — inside
tranche 3 (`tranche-3-extract-shim`, with its caller wired) and on
`t0567-ledger-ownership-guard` (`a85c918`, cut from tranche 2). Both guard
completion; they differ on what the guard compares, and tranche 3's is the
stronger of the two (see 0567's log for the reconciliation and the two
cases `claimed_input` cannot see). **Take tranche 3's side whole rather
than merging the two guards** — a merge that keeps both would carry two
signatures for the same method and a guard that reads as belt-and-braces
while actually being the weaker one's semantics.

The rest of the trial merge's claim — textual adjacency rather than
semantic disagreement in `ledger.ts` — is still to be verified on the real
merge rather than taken on trust.

## Relevant files

- Fork `src/features/search/conductor/ledger.ts` — the one conflicting
  file. Both sides append methods and schema DDL to the same class; the
  conflict is textual adjacency, not a semantic disagreement, as far as
  the trial merge showed. Verify that claim on the real merge rather
  than inheriting it from this sentence.
- Fork branches `tranche-3-extract-shim`, `tranche-schema-v2-content`,
  and their common parent `tranche-2-conductor-election`.

## Actions

1. Land 0553's two blockers first (its own ticket), so the merge carries
   no known defect forward.
2. Create the integration branch off `tranche-2-conductor-election`,
   merge both siblings into it, resolve `ledger.ts`.
3. Decide and record the going-forward convention: whether later
   tranches (0554, 0565, 0566) branch from this integration branch
   rather than from tranche 2, and whether the per-tranche branch rule
   in 0550 is amended to say so.

## Test

- The union of both branches' suites passes on the merged tree — not
  each branch's suite on its own branch. `vitest`, `tsc --noEmit`,
  `eslint` clean, as every tranche has reported.
- The schema branch's own migration test still passes against a v1 file
  brought forward, since the merge touches the DDL region.

## Verification

- [x] Every test from both branches present in the merged tree and green
      — 1 020 + 69 + 34 = 1 123, measured on each branch and on the merge
- [ ] The incumbent MiniLM byte-identical vector check green, per the
      tracker's standing invariant — NOT TICKED: no such check exists in
      the suite, and this merge touches no vector code. 0554 owns it

## Invariants

- v1's `search-index.sqlite` and its query path untouched.
- No behaviour change: this ticket resolves a merge, it does not fix or
  extend either side.

## Exit criteria

- [x] One fork branch holds tranches 1-3 and the v2 content schema —
      `conductor-integration`, c031478
- [x] Both suites green on it, with the test count reconciled
- [x] The branch convention for 0554/0565/0566 recorded (Action 3) —
      they branch from `conductor-integration`
